https://github.com/ethereum/eth2.0-specs/releases/tag/v0.12.2

There are, minimal semantic change as far as externally visible here:
- some function renaming;
- factoring out of `get_validator_from_deposit()` from `process_deposit()`
- splitting of phase 1 constants from phase 0 constants;
- addition of `DEPOSIT_CHAIN_ID` and `DEPOSIT_NETWORK_ID` constants;
- `get_committee_count_per_slot()` now only takes `Epoch`s instead of `Slot`s; and
- some edge-case fixing in `check_attestation()`/`process_attestation()`

As such, this remains compatible both in theory and empirically, for me, with `altona`, and this doesn't introduce any compile-time protocol-version-selection.

This PR largely doesn't address `p2p-interface` changes, which are for a separate PR.

